1
00:00:04,365 --> 00:00:12,655
Fill a cancelled slot from the waitlist — Scheduling ▸ Waitlist — Turn a cancellation into a booking instead of an empty hour.

2
00:00:18,052 --> 00:00:23,886
Scheduling ▸ Waitlist is everyone who wants an earlier slot than the one they have.

3
00:00:23,886 --> 00:00:30,785
Each entry carries the provider they need, the type of visit, and the days and times they can actually make.

4
00:00:30,785 --> 00:00:43,202
Priority and flexibility are what matter — the patient who can come any morning fills a gap the rigid one cannot.

5
00:00:43,202 --> 00:00:52,556
Switching to every status shows who has already been called, and who is booked.

6
00:00:52,556 --> 00:01:04,806
A slot has just opened. Notify contacts the next patient and marks the entry as called, so nobody rings them twice.

7
00:01:04,806 --> 00:01:12,024
Once they accept and you book them, mark the entry scheduled — it leaves the queue and the slot is filled.

8
00:01:12,024 --> 00:01:19,197
The habit that makes this work: put people on the waitlist with real availability, not just a name.

9
00:01:20,901 --> 00:01:35,381
What you just did

10
00:01:36,016 --> 00:01:45,016
Health | Efficiency | Growth — More in the Getting Started series — the next video is linked on screen.
